"_about": "Glycaemic index (glucose = 100) by food head. Values from the International Tables of Glycemic Index: IGT 2008 = Atkinson, Foster-Powell, Brand-Miller, Diabetes Care 2008;31:2281; IGT 2021 = Atkinson et al., Am J Clin Nutr 2021. Where the tables hold several entries the mean of the most representative one is used; `src` names the entry. `est: true` = analogue (a close relative in the tables), counted as estimated. Mappings are tried in file order, the first match wins; `name` is a regex on the food's name, `form` and `category` narrow further. Applied by pipeline/consumer/gi.py.",
"category_defaults_note": "grain..starchy_vegetable are the agreed defaults. vegetable (non-starchy: onion, tomato paste, carrot-like), nut_seed, condiment, meat, poultry, fish, egg, oil_fat and other are extensions for foods that reach 5 g available carbohydrate per 100 g (sauces, breaded or sweetened products, chestnuts); nuts and seeds are low GI so 15, the rest are composite foods so the prepared-food default 55.",
